      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Tracing & APM (OpenTelemetry)\n\n**Status: not yet landing.** This is the third SPOG pillar (metrics \u2713 \u00b7 logs \u2713 \u00b7 traces \u23f3), stubbed and ready to light up.\n\n### Current pipeline\n- The PWA emits client OTel spans (`app/src/lib/builder-shell-telemetry.ts`) but `VITE_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is unset \u2192 spans are **dropped**.\n- No OTel collector is deployed; no server-side instrumentation yet.\n\n### Intended (deferred prod-runtime work)\n1. Deploy an **OTel Collector** with the `googlecloud` exporter \u2192 **Cloud Trace**.\n2. Point `VITE_OTLP_ENDPOINT` at it \u2192 client traces land.\n3. Instrument octogee-api / gateway-edge / agent-run / shell-attach (OTLP \u2192 collector).\n\n### Where traces will be viewed\nCloud Trace is explored in the **GCP Cloud Console** (no reliable Grafana trace datasource plugin). Once span-metrics exist, RED panels + exemplars can be added below.\n\n\ud83d\udd17 [Cloud Trace console](https://console.cloud.google.com/traces/list?project=octogee)"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 18,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
